Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/opencontainers/runc v1.5.3

H-2 of the runc series: initProcess.start no longer speaks the C stage's
protocol. Upstream writes the bootstrap data to the init socket, reads the pid
of the final child from it, and waits for the first child to exit. With
runc-01-direct-init.patch the process the standard library started is init
itself, so those three steps are removed and its pid is used where the final
child's was.

The C stage also wrote the out-of-memory score of init from the bootstrap
data, and nothing in the Go init does. The parent writes it here, before it
sends init its configuration.

The reader, startInitialization, is unchanged: it decodes the init
configuration as JSON from the init socket and never read the bootstrap data,
so with that data gone the JSON is the first thing on the socket.

Needs runc-01-direct-init.patch: without it the started process is the C
stage's first parent, not init.

No upstream pull request is opened for this change: upstream keeps its C
stage, and the change is specific to a build with cgo off. The design is
docs/architecture/container/runtime.md.

Delete this series when Ze no longer vendors the runtime.

